Objective Statement

Formal Objective

The Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) shall generate adaptive decisions from the interpreted operating context by evaluating relevant conditions, available response alternatives, and applicable constraints, producing a decision representation suitable for subsequent authorization and execution.

---

Objective Intent

Establish the system's capability to transform an interpreted operating context into an appropriate adaptive decision while maintaining separation between decision generation, decision authorization, and physical action execution.

---

Success Criteria

This objective is considered satisfied when the system demonstrates the ability to:

- Evaluate relevant operating-context information.
- Identify and consider applicable response alternatives.
- Generate decisions appropriate to the interpreted operating context.
- Apply relevant decision constraints established by approved engineering artifacts.
- Represent the resulting decision in a form suitable for downstream authorization and execution.
- Maintain sufficient information to support traceability between the decision and the contextual conditions that informed it.

---

Engineering Constraints

- The objective shall remain solution-independent.
- The objective shall not prescribe a specific decision-making algorithm, model, planning technique, or implementation technology.
- Decision generation shall remain distinct from environmental perception and operating-context interpretation.
- Decision generation shall remain distinct from physical action execution.
- Generation of a decision shall not, by itself, imply authorization to execute that decision.
- Decision authority shall be established through approved architectural and governance mechanisms.
- Derived decision objectives shall remain traceable to SO-F-004.

---

Assumptions

- SO-F-003 provides an interpreted operating context.
- The operating context may contain uncertainty, incomplete information, or changing conditions.
- Applicable constraints and authority requirements may originate from other approved architectural elements.
- A downstream mechanism will determine whether a generated decision is authorized for execution.
- SO-F-005 is responsible for execution of an approved decision.
